<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adelasia of Torres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1207–1259</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adelasia of Torres was judge, or ruler, of the Judicate of Logudoro in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1236 until her death in 1259. Her first husband, Ubaldo Visconti, also ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallura">Gallura</a>; in 1238 she married Enzo, son of Emperor Frederick II, who took the title King of Sardinia. She died without heirs, and her realm was divided.</p></div>
